  "year": "1987",
  "subtitle": "A rubber-string guitar whose membrane fretboard hardwires each fret to a pitch — strum and fret, and the note is guaranteed",
  "why_scout_cares": "The consumer end of the MIDI-guitar spectrum, and a genuinely different interaction from the museum's SynthAxe: the DG-20 has no pitch-to-MIDI tracking at all. Nylon trigger strings and a rubber membrane fretboard where every fret contact is hardwired to a specific pitch — a pure switch matrix that eliminates tracking latency by construction. Commercially odd, mass-market, and the museum's only guitar-shaped membrane-switch instrument.",
  "search_terms": [
    "Casio DG-20 digital guitar",
